  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: jackson-core 2.11.3.rhlw-00005",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.11.3.rhlw-00005 with backported fixes for CVE-2025-52999 and CVE-2026-89425.\n\nCVE-2025-52999: jackson-core Has Potential for StackoverflowError if user parses an input file that contains very deeply nested data\n\nCVE-2026-89425: jackson-core: UTF8DataInputJsonParser._reportInvalidToken() does not honor maxErrorTokenLength, allowing unbounded StringBuilder growth\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core 2.11.3 from Maven Central.",
